.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_PKEY_DIGESTSIGN_SUPPORTS_DIGEST 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_PKEY_digestsign_supports_digest
.Nd indicate support for signature digest
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/evp.h
.Ft int
.Fo EVP_PKEY_digestsign_supports_digest
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *pkey"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "const char *name"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn EVP_PKEY_digestsign_supports_digest
function queries whether the message digest
.Fa name
is supported for public key signature operations associated with key
.Fa pkey .
The query is done within an optional library context
.Fa libctx
and with an optional property query
.Fa propq .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn EVP_PKEY_digestsign_supports_digest
function returns 1 if the message digest algorithm identified by
.Fa name
can be used for public key signature operations associated with key
.Fa pkey
and 0 if it cannot be used.
It returns a negative value for failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_DigestSignInit_ex 3 ,
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn EVP_PKEY_digestsign_supports_digest
function was added in OpenSSL 3.0.
